#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166865 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166718 :question/id #uuid "03bebdcd-5908-5c60-b35a-1c8f59593afd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9577" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f4f0de23892a6f76642f8c7e5d3a6112a8ffa2d9f50000cd974f293a7d8b3b6.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-1)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^2 + (y - (-1))^2 = 2^2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx^2 + (y+1)^2 = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049470 :topic/difficulty 1.147700024049995 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429503 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/